* =====================================================================
* client-board-channel-subcircuit.lib  --  one STIM channel (client-board-model.asc) as a subcircuit,
* plus the fixtures the T00..T13 test benches share.          2026-10-17
*
* Every test does:
*   .include client-board-models.lib
*   .include client-board-channel-subcircuit.lib
*
* With all parameters at their defaults, XSTIM is the S01 schematic
* exactly (T00 checks this against the S01 .op result).
* =====================================================================

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* STIM_CH  pins: INPUT (DAC / generator side of the board), LOAD (J1),
*                VRP, VRN (HV rails before the fuses).  J2 = global 0.
*
* Error terms the G op-amp models leave out, injected here (0 = off):
*   GE    INA149 gain error (fraction). Datasheet max 0.02 % -> 2e-4.
*         Folded into R7: I = V(INPUT)*(1+GE)/R7, which is what it does.
*   VOS2  INA149 output offset (V). Datasheet max 1.1 mV.
*   KCM   INA149 error per volt on REF (=LOAD); 90 dB CMRR -> 31.6e-6.
*         This is what sets the current source's output impedance.
*   KPS   op-amp supply rejection, input-referred V/V on the floating
*         rail (V(VP,VN) - 19.49 V). Not a datasheet number: tests that
*         use it say what they assume.
*   VOS1  TLE2141 offset (V). 0.9 mV max (non-A grade); 1.4 mV listed
*         by one distributor: the tests use 1.4 mV to stay conservative.
*   IB1   TLE2141 input bias current pulled out of LOAD (A). 1.5 uA max.
*   R7    sense resistor value; tests pass mc() tolerance through it.
*   TOLB  tolerance of the bias network resistors (R1..R6), mc() each.
*   VZ3, VZ4  zener knee shift; 2.74 = BZX84C5V1 nominal model.
*         +/-0.3 covers the 4.8..5.4 V spread of the part.
*
*   LGAC  AC amplitude of the loop-gain injection inside U2, between its
*         internal amplifier and its output pin (T15). 0 = no effect.
*   LGAC1 same for U1, between its output and REF (T15). 0 = no effect.
*   LGI   AC current injected into U2's output node (T15, Tian method). 0 = none.
*   GBWK, GBWK1  scale the gain-bandwidth of U2 / U1 (T18 loop-gain perturbation). 1 = datasheet.
*
* Fault switches (T11), 0 = healthy board:
*   FQ2CE  1 = Q2 collector-emitter short
*   FR3    1 = R3 open
*   FC1    1 = C1 short
*   FD1    1 = D1 open
*   FU1    1 = U1 output stuck at its + rail (REF pulled to VP)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt STIM_CH INPUT LOAD VRP VRN params: R7=1k TOLB=0 GE=0 VOS2=0 KCM=0 KPS=0
+ VOS1=0 IB1=0 VZ3=2.74 VZ4=2.74 FQ2CE=0 FR3=0 FC1=0 FD1=0 FU1=0 LGAC=0 LGAC1=0 LGI=0
+ GBWK=1 GBWK1=1
* rails: fuses and bulk caps on the board
RF1 VRP VCCP 0.5
RF2 VRN VCCN 0.5
C2 VCCP 0 1u
C3 VCCN 0 1u
* input clamp D3/D4 (BZX84C5V1, back to back)
XD3 dmid INPUT ZEN_BZX84 params: VZ={VZ3}
XD4 dmid 0 ZEN_BZX84 params: VZ={VZ4}
* bootstrapped floating supply
Q2 VCCP B2 VP MJD340
Q1 VCCN B1 VN MJD350
R1 VCCP n1 {mc(44.2k,TOLB)}
R2 n1 B2 {mc(44.2k,TOLB)}
R3 B2 a1 {if(FR3>0.5,1e12,mc(10k,TOLB))}
D1 a1 d1x BAS16
RD1 d1x OUT {if(FD1>0.5,1e12,1u)}
D2 OUT k2 BAS16
R4 k2 B1 {mc(10k,TOLB)}
R5 B1 n5 {mc(44.2k,TOLB)}
R6 n5 VCCN {mc(44.2k,TOLB)}
C1 B2 B1 100n
RFC1 B2 B1 {if(FC1>0.5,0.1,1e12)}
RFQ2 VCCP VP {if(FQ2CE>0.5,0.1,1e12)}
* U2 INA149 with its error terms in series with +IN
Berr u2p INPUT V={VOS2}+{KCM}*V(LOAD)+{KPS}*(V(VP,VN)-19.49)
XU2 u2p 0 REF REF VP VN OUT INA149GL params: LGAC={LGAC} LGI={LGI} GBWK={GBWK}
R7 OUT LOAD {R7/(1+GE)}
* U1 TLE2141 buffers LOAD onto REF
VOS1 u1p LOAD {VOS1}
XU1 u1p REF VP VN u1o TLE2141GL params: GBWK={GBWK1}
* loop-gain break for U1 (T15): 0 V DC; AC amplitude LGAC1
Vlg1 REF u1o 0 AC {LGAC1}
RFU1 REF VP {if(FU1>0.5,1,1e12)}
IB1 LOAD 0 {IB1}
.ends STIM_CH

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* INA149GL: INA149G (JY063_STIM_models.lib) with a loop-gain injection
* source between the internal amplifier and the VOUT pin, upstream of the
* 380k feedback resistor, so every feedback path of the current pump
* passes through it. LGAC=0 makes it identical to INA149G.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt INA149GL +IN -IN REF_A REF_B V+ V- VOUT params: LGAC=0 LGI=0 GBWK=1
R1   8 VOUT 380k
R2   -IN 8 380k
R3   +IN 9 380k
RREFA 9 REF_A 19k
RREFB REF_B 8 20k
XOP  9 8 V+ V- oo OPAGEN params: GBW={10.5Meg*GBWK} SR=5Meg IQ=0.81m VSWH=1.5 VSWL=1.5 AOL=1Meg
Vlg VOUT oo 0 AC {LGAC}
* current injection for the double-injection (Tian) loop-gain method
Ilg 0 VOUT 0 AC {LGI}
.ends INA149GL

* TLE2141GL: TLE2141G with its gain-bandwidth scaled by GBWK (1 = identical).
.subckt TLE2141GL IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT params: GBWK=1
XOP IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT OPAGEN params: GBW={5.9Meg*GBWK} SR=45Meg IQ=3.5m VSWH=1.0 VSWL=0.2 AOL=1Meg
.ends TLE2141GL

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* ZEN_BZX84: Diodes Inc. DI_BZX84C5V1 (in JY063_STIM_models.lib) with the
* internal knee voltage as a parameter.  VZ=2.74 is identical to it.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt ZEN_BZX84 1 2 params: VZ=2.74
D1 1 2 DF84
DZ 3 1 DR84
VZ 2 3 {VZ}
.model DF84 D ( IS=28.3p RS=33.9 N=1.10 CJO=66.2p VJ=0.750 M=0.330 TT=50.1n )
.model DR84 D ( IS=5.65f RS=44.5 N=3.00 )
.ends ZEN_BZX84

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* HEAD: dummy head between J1 (A) and J2 (B).
*   RS   tissue / phantom resistance
*   RE   each electrode-skin interface resistance (2 electrodes)
*   CE   each electrode-skin interface capacitance
*   CC   lead / cable capacitance across the output
* RE=1m CE=1p gives a pure resistor RS (the bench "electronic load").
* The electrode values are ASSUMPTIONS until the dummy head is measured;
* the tests sweep them over a wide range for that reason.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt HEAD A B params: RS=1k RE=1m CE=1p CC=1p
RS A e1 {RS}
RE1 e1 e2 {RE}
CE1 e1 e2 {CE}
RE2 e2 B {RE}
CE2 e2 B {CE}
CC A B {CC}
.ends HEAD

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* STIM_RAIL: behavioural rail load of one channel, for the HV converter
* simulation (power team).  Pins: VRP, VRN (rails), CMD (command voltage,
* 1 V = 1 mA, referred to 0).  RL = dummy-head load.  Checked against the
* full channel in T12.  Valid while the channel is inside compliance.
*   It, Ib : bias-string currents into / out of OUT (R1-R3, D1 / D2, R4-R6)
*   IQ     : U1 + U2 quiescent current, carried from VP to VN by Q2 / Q1
*   Iu     : U2 output current = load current - It + Ib, plus the INA149
*            internal 380k from its -IN (ground) to the ~0.95*V(LOAD) node
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt STIM_RAIL VRP VRN CMD params: RL=10k R7=1k IQ=4.31m
.param RB=98.4k
Bo vo 0 V=V(CMD)/1k*({RL}+{R7})
Bt it 0 V=max((V(VRP)-V(vo)-0.6)/{RB},0)
Bb ib 0 V=max((V(vo)-V(VRN)-0.6)/{RB},0)
Bu iu 0 V=V(CMD)/1k-V(it)+V(ib)+0.952*V(CMD)/1k*{RL}/380k
BP VRP 0 I=V(it)+{IQ}*min(max(V(VRP,VRN)/20,0),1)+max(V(iu),0)
BN 0 VRN I=V(ib)+{IQ}*min(max(V(VRP,VRN)/20,0),1)+max(-V(iu),0)
C2 VRP 0 1u
C3 VRN 0 1u
.ends STIM_RAIL
